@topic stdlib.std::abi::AbiIntegerBelowRange
title: -
summary: The declared error of a checked ABI creator (std::abi::i8 ... std::abi::usize) given an Int below its domain's minimum.
index: stdlib
keywords: below range; underflow; out of range; too small
related: stdlib.std::abi::AbiIntegerAboveRange stdlib.module.std::abi

== NOTES
A payload-free error of module abi, spelled std::abi::AbiIntegerBelowRange
in handlers and errors clauses outside it. A creator whose argument is
provably in range needs no handler; a provably out-of-range constant is
rejected as KNOWN-ERROR.

@topic stdlib.std::abi::AbiIntegerAboveRange
title: -
summary: The declared error of a checked ABI creator (std::abi::i8 ... std::abi::usize) given an Int above its domain's maximum.
index: stdlib
keywords: above range; overflow; out of range; too large
related: stdlib.std::abi::AbiIntegerBelowRange stdlib.module.std::abi

== NOTES
See stdlib.std::abi::AbiIntegerBelowRange: the same pair is shared by every
creator of the family, so the creator's name says which domain was
meant and the error which bound was violated.

