@topic stdlib.module.std::byte
title: -
summary: The Byte, Nibble, LowNibble and HighNibble integer domains, the checked conversion std::byte::from_int, nibble extraction, complement and std::byte::set.
index: stdlib
keywords: byte; nibble; bits; byte type; uint8
related: concept.integer-domains stdlib.bit_and stdlib.module.std::ascii

== NOTES
Ordinary Botlish over the bit primitives (bit_and, bit_or, bit_xor,
shift_left, shift_right): each function has a declared result domain the
compiler verifies. An Int becomes a std::byte::Byte where the compiler
proves its range (a comparison, a literal, a declared result) or through
std::byte::from_int. Outside the module, `import type std::byte::Byte` binds
the short type name. ASCII meaning is ascii::'s, not byte::'s.

@topic stdlib.std::byte::Byte
title: -
summary: The integer domain 0..255 (type Byte = Int in 0..255): a byte value, an ordinary Int proven in range.
index: stdlib
keywords: byte; uint8; octet; byte type; 0..255
related: stdlib.std::byte::from_int concept.integer-domains stdlib.std::str::encode_utf8 stdlib.std::abi::bytes::from_list

== NOTES
A Byte is an Int, so every Int operation applies, and its arithmetic is
Int arithmetic (a sum of two Bytes is an Int, not a wrapped Byte). An Int
enters the domain where the compiler proves 0 <= x <= 255 -- a literal, a
comparison guard, a function's declared `-> Byte` result -- or through
std::byte::from_int, which fails otherwise. std::str::encode_utf8 returns
List[Byte]; std::abi::bytes::from_list takes one.

@topic stdlib.std::byte::Nibble
title: -
summary: The integer domain 0..15 (a subtype of Byte): a logical 4-bit value.
index: stdlib
keywords: nibble; half byte; 4-bit value; hex digit value
related: stdlib.std::byte::nibble stdlib.std::byte::LowNibble stdlib.std::byte::HighNibble

@topic stdlib.std::byte::LowNibble
title: -
summary: The integer domain 0..15 for a nibble already positioned in the low half of a byte; nominally distinct from Nibble.
index: stdlib
keywords: low nibble; low half; lower 4 bits
related: stdlib.std::byte::low_nibble stdlib.std::byte::position_low stdlib.std::byte::Nibble

